Thank you. Thank you.

00:03:31.252 --> 00:03:32.587
My name is Tim Bernardes.

00:03:32.587 --> 00:03:35.048
I'm from São Paulo, Brazil, singer-songwriter.

00:03:35.465 --> 00:03:37.425
It's so cool to be here.

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:41.638
I love the show. I have been watching this, it's crazy, and thank you for being here.

00:03:43.097 --> 00:03:45.725
Thank you. Any Brazilians? Any Brazilians here?

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:48.686
There's always Brazilians, I love that.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:50.855
Good morning. Good afternoon. Good evening.

00:03:51.189 --> 00:04:01.908
So you know that? Last year I was invited to do the Tiny Desk Brasil. That was an edition that happened in São Paulo, my town.

00:04:01.991 --> 00:04:06.454
And I was just rehearsing a show with orchestra.

00:04:06.454 --> 00:04:14.587
We managed to put a bunch of orchestral players and now I wanted to do the opposite.

00:04:14.963 --> 00:04:20.093
The stripped-down that is actually my favorite way of playing, like, the solo thing.

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:23.429
So you can really focus on songwriting, not all this stuff.

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:29.185
And I'm gonna play some stuff I didn't play there and that I don't play often, so now I'm gonna play a song that I've never played live.

00:04:29.894 --> 00:04:35.066
That I'd done with BADBADNOTGOOD and the maestro Arthur Verocai from Brazil.

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:38.695
It's a song called "Poeira Cósmica."

00:05:07.515 --> 00:05:23.698
Night has fallen, there's a new moon over South America.

00:05:24.949 --> 00:05:35.918
A sign from the sky.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:39.547
Are we or are we not cosmic dust?

00:06:04.906 --> 00:06:14.916
Feel it in the wind, stardust.

00:06:16.209 --> 00:06:38.940
Time, all at once, there is more than what meets the eye in this life.

00:07:08.511 --> 00:07:14.183
I don't want to think anymore, I don't want to understand.

00:07:15.059 --> 00:07:20.731
Wherever I go, I feel without knowing.

00:07:21.065 --> 00:07:24.986
Unconsciously, I know there's some kind of mystery.

00:07:25.445 --> 00:07:42.420
And you've felt it, too, in the infinity of the soul.

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:49.260
Something more.

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:53.473
That we are not just cosmic dust.

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:25.296
Thank you.

00:08:29.675 --> 00:08:29.800
I'll sing a song now from my latest album that is called &lt;i&gt;Mil Coisas Invisíveis&lt;/i&gt;.

00:08:33.596 --> 00:08:40.394
It's a song that I wrote originally for Gal Costa, my great hero from Brazil.

00:08:40.686 --> 00:08:43.898
And she recorded this song and I recorded it on my own album.

00:08:44.232 --> 00:08:53.866
And I'm preparing a new album for next year, but I'm gonna play this one from the old album.

